   "B": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law and the public health law, in\nrelation to the definitions of industrial hemp, concentrated cannabis, and\nmarihuana",
    "basePrintNo": "S8072",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8072-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3302, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8072B\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to the definitions of\nconcentrated cannabis and marihuana\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to clarify the definitions of indus-\ntrial hemp, concentrated cannabis and marihuana.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Paragraph (a) of subdivision 4 of section 3302 of the public\nhealth law is amended.\n\nSection 2: Subdivision 21 of section 3302 of the public health law is\namended.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRecent events from across the State, have highlighted the need to clari-\nfy the definitions of concentrated cannabis and marihuana. This is\nintend to avoid confusion over products which utilize legal industrial\nhemp and its derivative by-products, distinguishing them from products\nwhich are illegal under NYS law.\n\nIndustrial hemp is defined in the New York State Agriculture and Markets\nlaw as the plant Cannabis sativa L. and any part of such plant, whether\ngrowing or not, with a delta-9 tetrahydrocannabional concentration of\nnot more than 0.3 percent on a dry weight basis.\n\nThis legislation clarifies and codifies the definitions of concentrated\nCannabis and marihuana as plants with a delta-9 tetrahydrocanabinol\nconcentration greater than 0.3  percent on a dry weight basis. AS a\nresult, law enforcement and others will have clearer guidance on ways to\ndetermine the differences.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis legislation will have no fiscal implications for State and Local\nGovernments.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
